1739	/// Clear the screen by scrolling its contents up into the scrollback,
1740	/// instead of erasing them. Everything up to and including the last
1741	/// non-empty row of the active area moves into history, so the user can
1742	/// still scroll back to see it. This is how "clear" behaves in many
1743	/// terminals and is what `Terminal.eraseDisplay(.scroll_complete)` uses.
1744	///
