    45	            // Linear blending weight correction corrects the alpha value to
    46	            // produce blending results which match gamma-incorrect blending.
    47	            if (use_linear_correction) {
    48	                // Short explanation of how this works:
    49	                //
    50	                // We get the luminances of the foreground and background colors,
    51	                // and then unlinearize them and perform blending on them. This
    52	                // gives us our desired luminance, which we derive our new alpha
    53	                // value from by mapping the range [bg_l, fg_l] to [0, 1], since
    54	                // our final blend will be a linear interpolation from bg to fg.
    55	                //
